  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young Women and Women with Disabilities and collectives with increased knowledge resources, tools and capacities to participate in local level advocacy on gender equality and elimination of SGBV</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young Women and Women with Disabilities and collectives learn and share knowledge resources, tools and capacities to participate in local level advocacy on gender equality and elimination of SGBV</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of knowledge resources, campaigns, products developed to advocate on gender equality and elimination of SGBV at all levels</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program would create knowledge resource that would help young women and women with disabilities effectively participate in advocacy</narrative>
    </description>
    <reference code="WRG049" indicator-uri="https://helpdesk-opendata-minbuza.nl/indicator-codelist/" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-01-01" value="0" year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the indicator measures any new values occurring since the start of the intervention,the baseline value is set at 0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="2">
      <location ref="Global"></location>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge resource produced through first hand research</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="2">
      <location ref="Global"></location>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">IWRAW AP design a CEDAW knowledge tool kit, which is intended as a knowledge resource for WGG partners to gain insight into the engaging with the CEDAW process. It talks about engaging with public informal processIWRAW AP also developed a manifesto &#x201c;Manifesto for Feminist Disability Justice in Global South&#x201d; based on collective inputs from partners for WGG ahead of the AWID feminist conference. This was supported by an online campaign with key messages around feminist disability justice.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1">
      <location ref="Global"></location>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge resource produced through first hand research</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="1">
      <location ref="Global"></location>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">IWRAW AP designed one knowledge resource on Transformative Justice as part of a virtual course on Access to Justice in in December 2023. The session on transformative justice will be focused on the different existing approaches to justice (punitive, restorative, etc.), and how it can be more transformative, and as a result more feminist in its approach. There session was attended by 25 participants from a) Grassroots organisations and activists working on access to justice and movement-building b) Development organisations working for the rights of women and socially excluded communities</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1">
      <location ref="Global"></location>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge resource produced through first hand research</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="1">
      <location ref="Global"></location>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">One knowledge resource was produced in December 2022 in the form of a framework on anti-carceral approaches to GBV and understanding international advocacy around WWDs and YW. The framework is expected to guide research for a briefing paper to practically implement anti-carceral thinking in our existing WGG work.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
